A re-proposed block that a signer had validated but never signed (for example one that moved from pre-committed to globally rejected on peers' rejections) was signed directly from the cached verdict, skipping the pre-commit threshold and the conflict checks. Such re-proposals now go back through the pre-commit evaluation (a block the group already signed only gets its pre-commit re-broadcast), an acceptance is only recreated for blocks the signer already signed, and chainstate re-check rejections now record their reason so a transient lookup error stays reconsiderable.
